Upstream-Name: gswitch-auto
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/vabuter/gswitch-auto/issues
Source: https://github.com/vabuter/gswitch-auto
Comment:
 gswitch-auto is a fork of gswitch (https://github.com/arumata/gswitch,
 MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 arumata) that adds automatic wrong-layout
 correction for the us/ru layout pair. The fork is distributed under the
 same MIT License. The embedded third-party material is described in
 /usr/share/doc/gswitch-auto/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md; the licence files
 installed next to it are the verbatim texts referenced below.

Files: *
Copyright: 2025 arumata
           2026 vabuter (gswitch-auto fork)
License: MIT

Files: internal/gswitch/lang/*
Copyright: 2026 netherguy4 (punto-rs)
           2026 vabuter (Go port, gswitch-auto fork)
License: MIT
Comment:
 Go port of the layout detector of punto-rs
 (https://github.com/rashevskyv/punto-rs: cli/src/layout.rs and
 cli/src/layout/keymap.rs, commit c836c87). The model files under
 internal/gswitch/lang/data/ and the test data
 internal/gswitch/lang/testdata/layout_cases.tsv are copied from punto-rs
 unchanged; the paragraphs below apply to the model files.

Files: internal/gswitch/lang/data/ru.bin
       internal/gswitch/lang/data/ru.bloom
Copyright: 1997-2008 Alexander I. Lebedev
           2026 netherguy4 (punto-rs, model build)
License: BSD-3-Clause-Modification
Comment:
 The Russian model embeds a modified form of the Russian hunspell dictionary
 (hunspell-ru 0.99g5): its word forms are stored as a Bloom filter (ru.bloom)
 and a letter-trigram model (ru.bin), built by punto-rs
 cli/scripts/build_layout_model.sh. These files are a derivative of the
 dictionary, not the dictionary itself, and are marked as modified here as
 the dictionary licence requires.

Files: internal/gswitch/lang/data/en.bin
       internal/gswitch/lang/data/en.bloom
Copyright: public domain (no copyright holder)
License: public-domain
 The English model is built from the word list of the Fedora "words"
 package (/usr/share/dict/words), which is in the public domain
 (SPDX: LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain).

Files: third_party/clipboard/*
Copyright: 2021 Changkun Ou <contact@changkun.de>
License: MIT
Comment:
 Vendored copy of golang.design/x/clipboard, carried over from upstream
 gswitch with its dlopen("libX11.so.6") fallback.

